--- With the GPU on, a view of a tensor placed there — a transpose, a slice
--- from the end — is its own numbers, and a number beside a tensor there
--- is one operation in both modes (spec, GPU Support): the view had been
--- read as the storage under it (`transpose[m]` was `m`, `slice[v, -2, 3]`
--- the first two), the compiled program had subtracted and divided on the
--- CPU where the interpreter did both on the GPU, so the two showed
--- different digits, and `sigmoid` and `softmax` with them. Where no GPU
--- answers, every tensor stays on the CPU and both modes agree there.
use math, math.nn

gpu[]
m = reshape[linspace[1.0, 4.0, 4], 2, 2]
log[transpose[m]]
log[transpose[m] * m]
log[exp[transpose[m]]]
v = linspace[1.0, 3.0, 3]
log[slice[v, -2, 3]]
log[sum[slice[v, 1, 3]]]
log[slice[v, -2, 3] + 1.0]
log[2.5 ./ v]
log[2.5 / v]
log[v - 0.5]
log[sigmoid[v]]
log[softmax[v]]
